Title: Harbor Light
Credit: written by
Author: Method Schedule contributors
Notes: A synthetic test script. Invented production, invented people.

INT. NET LOFT - NIGHT #1#

A cramped loft above the boatyard. Lamps swing. TOVE ANDERSEN (60s), weathered, mends a net by feel.

TOVE
Hand me the bigger needle.

KIT (O.S.)
Which one is bigger?

TOVE
The one you keep losing.

KIT climbs the ladder, needle in teeth.

EXT. BOATYARD - NIGHT #2#

Fog. A hull on blocks. KIT walks the length of it with a flashlight.

KIT
(to herself)
Forty feet. She said thirty.

EXT. HARBOR WALL - DAY #3#

Gulls. Morning sun. A FERRY horn somewhere out of sight.

/* An old version of this scene:
HARBORMASTER
No boats out today.
*/

HARBORMASTER LUND
You're Tove's niece.

KIT
Grand-niece.

HARBORMASTER LUND
Same trouble either way.

INT./EXT. KIT'S VAN - DAY #3A#

Kit drives, the net piled in the back. [[Check whether the van is a picture car.]]

CUT TO:

INT. NET LOFT - DAY #4#

Empty. The net hangs finished from the beams. A note pinned to it.

KIT (V.O.)
She left before I woke up.
